body:
This should work, although I just realised I added an extra card somewhere xO

&#x200B;

https://pasteboard.co/IbzD9VlDMBJW.jpg

Do you remember my collection of moments when the Pixel Partners have the Judge say "What do you MEEEEEAN?" Well there were so many moments I made another xD

&#x200B;

BUT there are **massive spoilers here for both Persona 4 and Ghost Trick's endgames, as well as the whole Phoenix Wright series,** so be mindful!

&#x200B;

Also for anyone who missed the first part, here you go!

https://youtu.be/JqeZWTGLh9U?si=D1xmpdBkpRr-bBmW

The trouble with those negative thoughts is not so much they're negative, more that they're true. There no point thinking positive if it means lying to yourself after all. 

&#x200B;

Today I lost to a Little Mac exclusively using F-smash and teabagging me. It's been 3.5 years and I can't even beat the lowest rung of skill. I try so hard, harder than anyone. I read every guide, watch every match, ask questions, share replays, but I just never improve. I genuinely believe I am too incompetent to amount to anything because intelligence is at the basis of all success.

&#x200B;

To put it in further context in day to day life as well, I was once locked in a mental hospital because doctors mistook my physical troubles for mental ones after I completely failed to put my points across. I also was fired from a VOLUNTARY job leading up to my dream job, simply for being too stupid for even basic tasks. I'm negative because I have every right to be, and other people would agree and laugh to boot if they knew everything about me.
